## 1. REQUIREMENTS ANALYSIS (Phase 1)

### Extraction Tables

**Functional Requirements:**
| ID | Requirement | Trigger | Input | Output | Priority |
|----|-------------|---------|-------|--------|----------|
| FR-01 | {action} | {when} | {data} | {result} | HIGH/MED/LOW |

**Non-Functional Requirements:**
| Category | Requirement | Metric | Target |
|----------|-------------|--------|--------|
| Performance | Response time | 95th percentile | < 500ms |
| Performance | Throughput | Records/min | 10,000+ |
| Reliability | Uptime | Monthly % | 99.9% |

**Integration Points:**
| System | Role | Protocol | Auth | Format | Volume |
|--------|------|----------|------|--------|--------|
| {name} | Source/Target | REST/SOAP/JDBC | OAuth/Basic | JSON/XML | {count}/day |

### Analysis Patterns

**Scan for:** Action verbs (sync, transfer), System names (Salesforce, SAP), Quantities (1000 records, daily), Quality (secure, reliable)

**Sample Data:** Identify field names, data types, nesting, date formats, null patterns

### Conversation vs Document

- **CONVERSATION**: Analysis, recommendations, questions, alternatives
- **DOCUMENT**: Clean decisions, tables, diagrams (match `examples/` format)

