## 2. ARCHITECTURE PATTERNS (Phase 2)

> **🚨 CRITICAL**: Present options with recommendation, WAIT for user approval before designing

### Architecture Decision Matrix

| Scenario | Recommended Pattern | Alternative |
|----------|---------------------|-------------|
| Simple sync (A → B) | System API Only | - |
| Sync with validation | System API Only | System + Process (if complex rules) |
| Multi-system orchestration | System + Process | Full API-Led (if multi-channel) |
| Multi-channel consumers | Full API-Led | System + Process (if limited reuse) |
| Large batch processing | System API + Batch | System + Process (if orchestration needed) |

### Pattern Descriptions (for Proposal)

**Pattern 1: System API Only**
- ✅ Minimal complexity, fastest to implement
- ✅ Lowest resource consumption
- ⚠️ Limited reusability, tight coupling
- **Best for:** Point-to-point, data sync, simple proxies

**Pattern 2: System + Process API**
- ✅ Business logic separation, reusable system APIs
- ⚠️ More components, slightly higher latency
- **Best for:** Order processing, multi-system orchestration

**Pattern 3: Full API-Led (3 Layers)**
- ✅ Maximum reusability, consumer-specific optimization
- ⚠️ Higher complexity, more development time
- **Best for:** Enterprise platforms, multi-channel apps

### Processing Strategy

| Volume | Strategy | Justification |
|--------|----------|---------------|
| 1-100 records | Real-Time | Low latency, immediate response |
| 100-1,000 | Real-Time or Batch | Depends on timing requirements |
| 1,000-10,000 | Batch | Optimize for throughput |
| 10,000+ | Batch with streaming | Memory efficiency, handle large files |

### Connector Selection

| System | Connector |
|--------|-----------|
| Salesforce | salesforce:* |
| SAP | sap:* |
| Oracle/MySQL/PostgreSQL | db:* |
| REST API | http:request |
| SOAP | wsc:consume |
| File/SFTP | file:*/sftp:* |
| Queue | anypoint-mq:*/jms:* |

