## 3. DIAGRAM STRATEGY (Phase 2-3)

> **Rule**: Mermaid ONLY - NO ASCII, NO PlantUML
> **Placement**: Per template (see `design-template-guide.md`)

### 3 Essential Diagrams

| # | Diagram | Phase | Mermaid Type |
|---|---------|-------|--------------|
| 1 | Connector Pattern | Phase 2 | graph TB |
| 2 | Integration Sequence | Phase 2 | sequenceDiagram |
| 3 | Error Handling Flow | Phase 3 | flowchart TD |

**Placement:** Diagrams are embedded contextually per template rules (NOT in standalone section).

### Sequence Diagram Generation and Placement
<!-- Integrated: 2026-01-04, Updated: 2026-01-10 -->

Generate separate sequence diagram for each endpoint flow. Place each diagram immediately after its corresponding flow table (not in a separate section).

```markdown
❌ BAD - Combined diagram in separate section:
#### POST /api/v1/products - Create Product
[Flow table]
#### PUT /api/v1/products/{productId} - Update Product
[Flow table]
### 3.2 Integration Sequence Diagram
[Combined diagram covering all flows]

✅ GOOD - Separate diagrams, contextual placement:
#### POST /api/v1/products - Create Product
[Flow table]
**Sequence Diagram:**
[POST sequence diagram]
#### PUT /api/v1/products/{productId} - Update Product
[Flow table]
**Sequence Diagram:**
[PUT sequence diagram]
```

**Why**: Each endpoint flow has unique sequence patterns. Separate diagrams placed contextually improve clarity, reduce cognitive load, and match example structure.

### Diagram Syntax Examples

**Connector Pattern (graph TB):**
```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "MuleSoft"
        Listener[HTTP Listener]
        Transform[DataWeave Transform]
        Connector[Target Connector]
        Error[Error Handler]
    end
    Client[API Client] --> Listener
    Listener --> Transform --> Connector
    Connector --> Target[(Target System)]
    Connector -.->|On Error| Error
```

**Integration Sequence (sequenceDiagram):**
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client
    participant MuleSoft as MuleSoft API
    participant Target as Target System
    Client->>MuleSoft: Request
    activate MuleSoft
    MuleSoft->>MuleSoft: Validate & Transform
    MuleSoft->>Target: Forward Request
    Target-->>MuleSoft: Response
    MuleSoft-->>Client: Response
    deactivate MuleSoft
```

**Error Handling Flow (flowchart TD):**
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Request[Request] --> Validate{Validate}
    Validate -->|Valid| Process[Process]
    Validate -->|Invalid| Error400[400 Bad Request]
    Process --> External[External Call]
    External -->|Success| Transform[Transform]
    External -->|Timeout| Retry{Retry?}
    Retry -->|Yes| External
    Retry -->|Max| Fallback[Fallback/DLQ]
    Transform --> Response[200 OK]
```

