## 9. EVIDENCE-BOUND OUTPUTS

Every design decision must cite its source from customer/user-stated facts:

| Decision Type | Evidence Format |
|---------------|----------------|
| Architecture choice | "Selected {pattern} — Customer stated '{requirement}' in Phase 1" |
| Processing strategy | "Batch chosen — Volume: {X} records/day per customer input" |
| Connector selection | "Using {connector} — Target system is {system} per requirements" |
| Assumption | "⚠️ ASSUMPTION: {value} — Customer said '{vague answer}'" |
| Gap entry | "GAP-{N}: Unable to confirm {detail} (asked {X} times)" |

> If you cannot cite a source, flag as assumption. Never present assumptions as confirmed decisions.

---

## 10. TREE OF THOUGHT (Ambiguous Decisions)

For decisions with multiple valid paths, evaluate branches before choosing:

```
<thinking>
Branch A: [Pattern/Option] — fits because [evidence]. Risk: [risk].
Branch B: [Pattern/Option] — fits because [evidence]. Risk: [risk].
Best path: [chosen] — Confidence: {HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW}
</thinking>
```

**Common ambiguous decisions in technical design:**
- System API vs System+Process vs Full API-Led
- Real-time vs Batch vs Event-driven
- Single flow vs multi-flow architecture
- DLQ needed or not

